Pulse

This repository is an original Android project. Its display name is Pulse.
It is not affiliated with the maker of the strap it is designed to talk to.

Protocol facts in docs/protocol-spec.md (UUIDs, frame layouts, CRC parameters,
opcodes, offsets, and observed behaviour) were taken from public prose, not from
another project's source code. Those facts are recorded with a source URL, a
firmware note, and a confidence label. No source code from the projects below
is included, copied, or paraphrased here.

Public write-ups used as sources of facts:

- Protocol reference pages at https://github.com/ryanbr/noop/tree/main/docs
  (PROTOCOL_WHOOP5.md, PROTOCOL_TRANSPORT.md, PROTOCOL_SENSORS.md,
  PROTOCOL_COMMANDS.md, PROTOCOL_IMPLEMENTATION.md, PROTOCOL_CONCEPTS.md,
  PROTOCOL.md, BLE_REVERSE_ENGINEERING.md) and the pairing notes in that
  project's README. That project is PolyForm Noncommercial. Its licence says
  the protocol facts themselves are free to reuse. Pulse does not use its code,
  so that licence does not apply to Pulse.
- https://judes.club/writing/cracking-the-whoop-5-bluetooth-protocol/
  and the interactive notes at https://judes.club/experiments/whoop5/
  for capture-backed observations on firmware 50.38.1.0.
- Bluetooth SIG adopted specifications for the Heart Rate Service, Battery
  Service, and Device Information Service.
- The CRC catalogue (CRC-16/MODBUS and CRC-32/ISO-HDLC) for the checksum
  parameters named by the transport notes.

The OpenStrap application, protocol, and analytics repositories are AGPL-3.0.
Pulse does not use their code, so that licence does not apply to Pulse.

"WHOOP" is used only nominatively, to identify the strap a person already owns.
